=== Memory Management Edge Case Tests ===

These tests verify error handling and edge cases:
1. Freeing NULL pointer
2. Freeing with wrong size
3. Double-free scenarios
4. Zero-size allocation
5. Very large allocation
6. Memory alignment expectations
7. Concurrent multiple allocations

=== Test: Freeing NULL Pointer ===

Phase 1: Attempting to free NULL pointer
  mulle_mmap_free_pages(NULL, 4096) returned: 0
  SUCCESS: Function handled NULL pointer gracefully
Test completed

=== Test: Freeing With Wrong Size ===

System page size: 65536 bytes
Allocating: 131072 bytes (2 pages)
Phase 1: Allocating pages
  SUCCESS: Allocated 131072 bytes
Phase 2: Attempting to free with wrong size
  Attempting to free 65536 bytes (wrong size - should be 131072)
  mulle_mmap_free_pages() with wrong size returned: 0
  INFO: Function accepted wrong size (implementation-dependent behavior)
  Pages may have been partially freed
  Attempting to free remaining part
  Free remaining returned: 1
Test completed

=== Test: Double Free Scenarios ===

System page size: 65536 bytes
Phase 1: Allocating page
  SUCCESS: Allocated 65536 bytes
Phase 2: First free
  First free returned: 0
  SUCCESS: First free succeeded
Phase 3: Attempting double free
  Double free returned: 1
  GOOD: Double free detected and rejected (errno: Success)
Test completed

=== Test: Zero Size Allocation ===

Phase 1: Attempting to allocate 0 bytes
  INFO: Zero-size allocation returned NULL (errno: Success)
  This is typical behavior for zero-size allocations
Test completed

=== Test: Very Large Allocation ===

Phase 1: Attempting to allocate very large size
  Requesting: 9223372036854775807 bytes (SIZE_MAX/2)
  GOOD: Very large allocation rejected (errno: Success)
  System correctly enforced resource limits
Test completed

